# Ignore absolutely everything by default to prevent accidental commits
# This acts as a primary security layer against binaries and IDE configuration files.
*

# Un-ignore directories so Git can actually traverse the project folders
# Without this, Git will not be able to scan subdirectories for our whitelisted files.
!*/

# Explicitly un-ignore required C++ source and header files
# These are the exclusive code artifacts permitted for compilation and grading.
!*.cpp
!*.h

# Un-ignore documentation and version control configuration
# The markdown files are required for the README and AI essay, while the gitignore itself must be tracked.
!*.md
!.gitignore